# Public environment variables (SolarBharat Next.js app)

Copy to `.env.local` (never commit secrets):

```bash
# Canonical site URL for sitemap, metadata, and Open Graph (no trailing slash)
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://solarbharat.in

# GitHub Pages project deploy only — leading slash, repo name (e.g. /Solcore).
# Leave empty for Vercel or user-site repos (<user>.github.io).
NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_PATH=

# Optional — PostHog product analytics (plan §10.4)
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=
# Optional — default is PostHog Cloud US
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=https://app.posthog.com

# Phase 2 — NREL PVWatts / NSRDB (plan §6.1). When set, /api/solar prefers this over NASA POWER.
# https://developer.nrel.gov/signup/
NREL_API_KEY=

# Phase 2 — Supabase (plan §10.2). Optional until auth / directory ship.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Public support inbox — shown on /contact as a mailto link (not a secret).
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPPORT_EMAIL=

# --- Phase 2 ops (cron + moderation + email) — see docs/OPS_PHASE2.md ---
# Server-only: never expose in NEXT_PUBLIC_* or client bundles.
CRON_SECRET=
MODERATION_SECRET=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Resend — double opt-in for /alerts (POST /api/cron/send-alert-confirmations)
RESEND_API_KEY=
RESEND_FROM_EMAIL=

# Optional: POST /api/cron/quota-ingest with empty body inserts demo row
QUOTA_INGEST_SEED=

# Server-only: expose /preview/moderation UI in middleware (default off)
ENABLE_MODERATION_UI=

# --- Static export (GitHub Pages) — see docs/OPS_STATIC_EXPORT.md ---
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_PATH=/YourRepoName
# API routes, middleware, cron, and rate limits are NOT in static out/ — use Supabase anon for forms.
```

Vercel: add the same keys under **Project → Settings → Environment Variables**.
